=TITLE Changelog

=begin pod :released-in<upcoming>
=head2 Upcoming

=end pod

=begin pod :released-in<0.9.0>
=head2 0.9.0 — 2026-08-14

=item pass the file type to the editor, so a Markdown file is highlighted as Markdown and a Podlite file as Podlite
=item open Markdown files (C<.md>, C<.markdown>, C<.mkdn>, C<.mkd>, C<.mdown>) and render them as Markdown in the preview; added file associations so double-click and drag-and-drop open them
=item the editor reads the document as a tree now: every markup code is coloured, section names and your own block names read apart from standard ones, settings inside a markdown fence are coloured, and C«G<>» content shows as a covered strip that opens under the caret
=item a block that fails to render no longer blanks the preview — it degrades to a small placeholder and the rest of the page stays
=item render the C«W<>» contextual link, entity codes inside an inline C«C<>» code, and a table written inside a cell as a grid
=item recognise the C<=set> directive, which passes settings to the block that follows it

=end pod

=begin pod :released-in<0.8.4>
=head2 0.8.4

=head3 Fixed

=item C<=boundary> no longer crashes the live preview — the renderer was passing children to a C«<hr>» element, which React 18+ rejects on void-element tags. The bare directive (C<=boundary>), the abbreviated form with inline content (C<=boundary Text>), and C<=boundary :caption(…)> all render as a void C«<hr/>» now (L<#70|https://github.com/podlite/podlite-desktop/issues/70>)
=item C<=Mermaid> diagrams render again on the current mermaid release — the diagram plugin moved off the deprecated callback C<render> and C<init> APIs that started failing on mermaid 11

=head3 Security

=item bump electron to 39.8.5 (resolves four use-after-free / command-line switch injection advisories)
=item bump electron-updater to 6.8 (resolves windows code-signing bypass advisory)
=item bump webpack to ^5.76 (resolves cross-realm object access advisory)
=item bump transitive deps: lodash, follow-redirects, serialize-javascript, tmp, postcss, shell-quote, js-yaml, tar, @tootallnate/once

=head3 Changed

=item replace electron-builder-notarize with @electron/notarize using notarytool (the deprecated altool path no longer accepts submissions)

=end pod

=begin pod :released-in<0.8.3>
=head2 0.8.3

=head3 Changed

=item macOS distribution ships separate arm64 and x64 builds; Apple Silicon users get native performance instead of running through Rosetta 2

=head3 Fixed

=item C<=picture> now renders in the live preview on the Mac App Store build — image bytes are read in the main process and inlined as a base64 data URL, so the renderer doesn't depend on C<file://> access that the sandbox denies for sibling files
=item numbered lists from C<=config item1 :numbered> — items now render as an ordered list (C<1.> C<2.> C<3.>) instead of bullets (L<#61|https://github.com/podlite/podlite-desktop/issues/61>)
=item C<=code> blocks with C«:lang<…>» attribute are syntax-highlighted in the live preview, matching the editor pane. Inline formatting codes inside C<=code> (when C«:allow<…>» is set) layer on top — C«B<…>» becomes bold, C«I<…>» becomes italic, C«C<…>» becomes inline code, with the highlighter's colors preserved underneath (L<#62|https://github.com/podlite/podlite-desktop/issues/62>)

=end pod

=begin pod :released-in<0.8.2>
=head2 0.8.2

=head3 Fixed

=item file watcher no longer crashes the app when the OS denies recursive directory watching (Mac App Store sandbox, iCloud Drive folders, Windows AppX) — auto-reload silently disables for that document instead (L<#60|https://github.com/podlite/podlite-desktop/issues/60>)

=end pod

=begin pod :released-in<0.8.1>
=head2 0.8.1

=head3 Fixed

=item C<=Mermaid> block no longer crashes the live preview while you type — the renderer now handles empty/transient block content gracefully

=end pod

=begin pod :released-in<0.8.0>
=head2 0.8.0

=head3 New

=item inline image paste and drag-drop — clipboard images and dropped files save to a C<media/> folder next to the current document and insert C«=picture media/<name>»; dropping a file that already lives in that folder references it in place without copying
=item C<=include> resolves in the preview at render time — fs reader against current document's directory with C<mtime> cache; recursive watcher invalidates cache and re-renders when included files change externally
=item glob patterns in C<=include> (e.g. C<=include file:**/*.podlite | defn>) expand via depth-bounded directory walk, skipping dotfiles
=item automatic numbering for C<:numbered> headings — renders as C<N.M.K.> prefix; respects C<=config head1 :numbered> defaults and C<:!numbered> per-block override

=head3 Fixed

=item double window on launch when opening a file from Finder or by drag-onto-icon (L<#57|https://github.com/podlite/podlite-desktop/issues/57>)
=item C<File → Open> no longer replaces the currently-open document — opens the new file in a fresh window; empty untitled windows still accept the opened file in place (L<#56|https://github.com/podlite/podlite-desktop/issues/56>)
=item C<Cmd+S> on an untitled document now opens the Save-As dialog instead of doing nothing (L<#55|https://github.com/podlite/podlite-desktop/issues/55>)
=item C<=picture> rendering in the preview pane — the previous C<file:///> protocol handler stripped the leading slash; absolute and relative-to-document paths both display correctly (L<#58|https://github.com/podlite/podlite-desktop/issues/58>)
=item external-edit reload after atomic writes (IDE autosave, sync tools) — watch the parent directory instead of the file
=item performance: attach IPC listeners once per mount instead of every render

=head3 Spec conformance (via `@podlite/*` libs rebuild)

=item C<:folded> on C<=head> now folds the whole section recursively, including headings inside C<=begin nested>/C<=defn>/etc.
=item C<=config> block preconfiguration (C<=config head1 :folded>, C«=config code :lang<python>») is now applied at render time — previously parsed but ignored
=item single-letter C<=alias> identifiers (C<=alias X foo> → C«A<X>») now accepted per spec
=item C<=alias> no longer leaks state into the next C<=begin>/C<=end> block's syntax highlighting
=item C<=TITLE>/C<=NAME>/C<=SYNOPSIS>/C<=Diagram> and other semantic/custom blocks in abbreviated form recognised by the editor highlighter
=item C<=row>, C<=cell>, C<=data-table>, C<=boundary>, C<=set>, C«G<>», C<:masked> recognised in the editor highlighter (spec v2.0)

=head3 Acknowledgements

Several of this release's fixes started as a detailed bug report by L<@schueani|https://github.com/schueani> in L<#53|https://github.com/podlite/podlite-desktop/issues/53> — thanks for the careful diagnosis and follow-up.

=end pod

=begin pod :released-in<0.7.2>
=head2 0.7.2

=item fix snap Wayland crash on Ubuntu 24.04 — enable C<allowNativeWayland> to prevent C<DISABLE_WAYLAND=1> injection by electron-builder (L<#43|https://github.com/podlite/podlite-desktop/issues/43>)

=end pod

=begin pod :released-in<0.7.1>
=head2 0.7.1

=item syntax highlighting for code blocks in preview (L<#42|https://github.com/podlite/podlite-desktop/issues/42>)
=item snap: add Wayland support — C<wayland> plug + C<ELECTRON_OZONE_PLATFORM_HINT=auto> (L<#43|https://github.com/podlite/podlite-desktop/issues/43>)

=end pod

=begin pod :released-in<0.7.0>
=head2 0.7.0

=head3 New

=item code folding for C<=begin>/C<=end> blocks and C<=head> sections (Ctrl-Shift-[ / Ctrl-Shift-])
=item list continuation on Enter — auto-insert C<=item> with preserved type prefix (C<[ ]>, C<#>)
=item Tab/Shift-Tab to change C<=item> nesting level
=item auto-reload file when changed on disk (silent or with dialog)
=item "Open Files in Preview" toggle in View menu
=item per-file view mode persistence across sessions (editor/preview/split)
=item restore editor state between sessions (cursor, scroll, fold state)
=item "Copy as PNG" for preview content

=head3 Fixed

=item editor input latency reduced from 860ms to near-zero per keystroke
=item search panel disappearing after Enter on first result
=item links not opening from preview panel (Electron 38 compatibility)
=item crash when opening a directory path instead of a file
=item cursor not visible on new window open
=item fold markers appearing inside verbatim blocks (C<=code>, C<=comment>, C<=data>)

=end pod

=begin pod :released-in<0.6.1>
=head2 0.6.1

=item editor refactored and rebuilt using updated libraries
=item added syntax highlighting for Podlite markup language
=item refactored key bindings
=item refactored window open/save/new workflow
=item fixed duplicate file opening issues
=item added C<=markdown> standard block support
=item added text search (C<Cmd-F>)
=item added new blocks: C<=Mermaid>, C<=picture>
=item added ability to open URLs from editor using C«L<>» links (C<Cmd>/C<Win> or C<Ctrl> modifier)
=item added C<file:> schema support in C«L<>» links - opens files in new editor window
=item half-screen preview toggle — C<Ctrl> + C<.> / C<Cmd> + C<.>
=item full-screen preview toggle — C<Ctrl> + C<\> / C<Cmd> + C<\>
=item added inline text style support (bold C«B<>», italic C«I<>», code C«C<>», links C«L<>», strikethrough C«O<>») within paragraphs and table cells
=item fixed redraw issue when resizing the application window
=item improved code block visibility in CSS
=item fixed build configuration to support macOS 26 (Thaoe)

=end pod

